# Start
- Validate Something
// `X` is a gateway node. Since we want two split execution
// into multiple sequence flows, we cannot simply continue
// writing statements. Instead, we use an arrow `->` with
// a label of your choice, in this case `val`, to tell that
// this specific sequence flow continues somewhere else.
// Look for matching `<-val` below.
X Validation Result ->val

// This is the first continuation of the sequence flow.
// The display text on the edge is written as free-form text
// behind the arrow+label.
- Appreciate the effort <-val Failed
! End

// At this point, the previous sequence flow has been completed
// (through the `! End` statement).
// This means, we can catch up the `->val` sequence flow
// a further time. Now, we use another edge display text.
- Incorporate <-val Success
. End

// You could continue adding more branches to the gateway
// by adding more statements with the `<-val` arrow.
